.TH FOREST-SCREENSHOT 1 "November 2026" "forest" "Forest desktop environment"
.SH NAME
forest-screenshot \- take a screenshot in the Forest desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forest-screenshot
.RB [ \-\-full " | " \-\-monitor
.RI [ NAME "] | " \-\-window " | " \-\-region ]
.RB [ \-\-delay
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-save ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-clipboard ]
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without a capture mode,
.B forest-screenshot
opens a small dialog with one button per mode. Its delay and save/clipboard
choices are remembered.
With a mode it captures immediately, for hotkeys and scripts.
.PP
The image is saved to
.I Screenshots
under the XDG pictures directory as
.IR Screenshot_YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS.png ,
copied to the clipboard as image/png, and announced with a desktop
notification.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-full
Capture all outputs, composited by position.
.TP
.BR \-\-monitor " [" \fINAME\fR ]
Capture the named output, or pick one by clicking it.
.TP
.B \-\-window
Capture the active window.
.TP
.B \-\-region
Drag a rectangle on a frozen, dimmed copy of the screen. Enter or a
double-click confirms; Esc cancels without error.
.TP
.BI \-\-delay " N"
Wait N seconds before capturing.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-save
Only copy to the clipboard.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-clipboard
Only save the file.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE"
Save to FILE instead of the Screenshots directory.
.SH BUGS
On scaled outputs the compositor renders window captures at logical size, so
.B \-\-window
images are smaller than the other modes; capture the output and crop for full
resolution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forest (1)
